### On what specific date did the shooting incident occur in Kenosha, Wisconsin, for which Kyle Rittenhouse was accused?
Answer: The shooting incident occurred on Tuesday, August 25, 2020.

Source URL: https://www.thedailybeast.com/kyle-rittenhouse-17-year-old-suspect-charged-with-murder-after-two-killed-at-kenosha-protest

### How many people were killed in the Kenosha shooting incident on that date?
Answer: According to the search result, **two people were killed** in the Kenosha shooting incident, and a third person was wounded with serious but not life-threatening injuries. As the article states: "Two people were killed, and a third was hospitalized with serious, but not life-threatening injuries, the Kenosha Police Department said in a statement."

Source URL: https://www.foxnews.com/us/jacob-blake-kenosha-wisconsin-protest-shooting-militia

### What were the identities of the individuals killed in the Kenosha shooting incident?
Answer: The two individuals killed in the Kenosha shooting incident were **Anthony Huber**, a 26-year-old from Silver Lake, Wisconsin, who was described as a talented skateboarder, and **Joseph Rosenbaum**, a 36-year-old originally from Waco, Texas who had recently moved to Kenosha to be close to his daughter. As the source notes, Huber "was shot while attacking the shooter with his skateboard in order to save another person from being shot," while Rosenbaum was described by his sister as "the goofy and crazy man who he was."

Source URL: https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2020/8/27/what-we-know-about-the-victims-of-the-kenosha-shooting

### What specific criminal charges, if any, were officially filed against Kyle Rittenhouse by the Kenosha County District Attorney in relation to the shootings?
Answer: Based on the search result, the Kenosha County District Attorney officially filed multiple criminal charges against Kyle Rittenhouse. These included "two counts of first-degree intentional homicide, as well as first-degree reckless homicide and attempted first-degree intentional homicide." He also faced "two charges of reckless endangerment, which are also felony counts, and a misdemeanor count of possession of a dangerous weapon under the age of 18."

Source URL: https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/suspect-jacob-blake-protest-shooting-appear-court-extradition-hearing-n1238502

### What was the official stated purpose or cause of the protest gathering that was occurring in Kenosha, Wisconsin, at the time of the shooting?
Answer: The official stated purpose of the protests in Kenosha was in response to the police shooting of Jacob Blake, a Black man, who was shot seven times in the back by a Kenosha police officer on Sunday, August 23, 2020. As the source states, "This week's protests have been in response to Kenosha police severely wounding a Black man, Jacob Blake, Sunday afternoon after responding to what police say was a domestic incident." The city had become part of a broader "summer of unrest and calls for racial justice" nationwide.

